 whose voluminous translations have won widespread acclaim, here presents selected discourses of the Buddha from the Pali Canon, the earliest record of what the Buddha taught. Divided into ten thematic chapters, In the Buddha's Words reveals the full scope of the Buddha's discourses, from family life and marriage to renunciation and the path of insight. A concise informative introduction precedes each chapter, guiding the reader toward a deeper understanding of the texts that follow.\" \"In the Buddha's Words allows even readers unacquainted with Buddhism to grasp the significance of the Buddha's contributions to our world heritage. Taken as a whole, these texts bear eloquent testimony to the breadth and intelligence of the Buddha's teachings, and point the way to an ancient yet ever vital path. Students and seekers alike will find this systematic presentation indispensable.\"--Jacket."},"latest_revision":19,"revision":19,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-20T12:32:48.126070"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-10-27T16:53:45.402152"}}},"ISBN:9781681722733":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781681722733","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL39214796M/The_Dhammapada","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL39214796M/The_Dhammapada","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"title":"The Dhammapada","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL9705642A","name":"Acharya Buddharakkhita"},{"key":"/authors/OL2780105A","name":"Bhikkhu Bodhi"}],"publish_date":"Sep 23, 2019","source_records":["amazon:1681722739"],"number_of_pages":156,"publishers":["BPS Pariyatti Editions"],"isbn_10":["1681722739"],"isbn_13":["9781681722733"],"physical_format":"paperback","full_title":"The Dhammapada The Buddha's Path of Wisdom","subtitle":"The Buddha's Path of Wisdom","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Source title: The Dhammapada: The Buddha's Path of Wisdom"},"works":[{"key":"/works/OL28600181W"}],"key":"/books/OL39214796M","latest_revision":1,"revis